body:
## Purpose

Owner directive: engineering-quality control must be a formal PM responsibility, not something the owner must remember or design manually.

This governance-only change updates `governance/prompts/AIOS_CORE_PM_HANDOFF_2026-09-24.md` to make the following mandatory for code/executable engineering tasks:

- fresh exact baseline / identity before work;
- root-cause analysis before repair;
- RED-before-GREEN when feasible, with preserved RED evidence;
- explicit invariants, allowed paths and forbidden scope;
- minimal patch / no opportunistic refactor;
- author targeted + regression + applicable failure-path testing;
- author cannot self-accept or merge;
- Fresh Independent Acceptance in a separate window;
- acceptance window cannot repair its own findings;
- PM fresh adjudication before integration;
- strict separation of CODE_WRITTEN / TESTS_GREEN / REVIEW_READY / ACCEPTANCE_PASS / PM_INTEGRATED / REAL_EXECUTION_COMPLETE / SEMANTIC_PASS;
- fail-closed handling for identity/evidence/scope uncertainty;
- PM owns standalone handoff prompt quality;
- routine Git/test/CI/evidence mechanics stay with PM; owner escalation is reserved for product intent, risk and true owner decisions.

## Scope

- Governance/prompt only.
- 1 file changed.
- No `src/**`, `tests/**`, workflow, package, C15, Resident, evaluator, UI/hardware changes.
- No change to current RC004 execution state.

## Integration boundary

**DO NOT MERGE** in this PR creation window. Review/integration remains a separate PM action.
